I can help — this is a good set of things to prepare before your annual physical. A few quick clarifying questions first so my suggestions are accurate:
- Can you confirm your sex (male or female)? Menopause status matters for osteopenia decisions.
- Can you confirm your current medications and doses? (You wrote “hypertension (metformin 500 mg twice daily)” and “GERD (metoprolol 25 mg)” — metformin treats diabetes and metoprolol treats blood pressure/heart disease, so I want the exact meds.)
- When you said “my last blood pressure was 28” — do you mean 128, 128/??, or something else?
